---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '@/config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`Privacy Policy for ${siteConfig.siteName}: client-side calculators, cookies, Google AdSense, and analytics disclosures.`}
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated: 2026-10-19</em></p>
  <p class="answer-first">
    Calculator inputs stay in your browser. We do not upload payment amounts to our servers. If the site owner later
    enables Google Analytics or Google AdSense, those services may set cookies as described below.
  </p>
  <h2>Information we process</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Calculator usage:</strong> amounts and fee options are processed locally in JavaScript on your device.</li>
    <li><strong>Essential preferences:</strong> cookie-notice acknowledgement stored in localStorage.</li>
    <li><strong>Contact email:</strong> if you email us, we receive the content of your message.</li>
    <li><strong>Hosting logs:</strong> standard request logs (IP, user agent) may be collected by the hosting provider.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Google AdSense and advertising cookies</h2>
  <p>
    When AdSense is enabled, Google and third-party vendors use cookies to serve ads based on prior visits to this and
    other websites. Google’s use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your visits.
    You can opt out of personalized advertising by visiting{' '}
    <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Ads Settings</a>
    or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">www.aboutads.info</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies such as the DoubleClick cookie to serve ads. Personalized ads in
    the EEA, UK, and Switzerland require a Google-certified consent management platform (CMP) integrated with the IAB
    TCF. The site owner must configure a CMP before enabling personalized ads in those regions.
  </p>
  <h2>Google Analytics (GA4)</h2>
  <p>
    If a GA4 measurement ID is configured, Google Analytics may collect pseudonymous usage data (pages viewed, device
    category, approximate geo). IP anonymization should remain enabled. You can block analytics with browser controls or
    opt-out extensions.
  </p>
  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This site is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy questions: <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
